---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
const updated = 'October 2026';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Settings — Minar-e-Pakistan Visitor Guide"
  description="Understand the cookies this independent Minar-e-Pakistan guide uses, why, and how to manage your preferences in your browser."
  updated={updated}
>
  <section class="topic-section">
    <h2>What cookies are</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small text files placed on your device by websites you visit. They help sites remember your preferences and understand how the site is used. You can delete or block cookies in your browser settings at any time.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="topic-section">
    <h2>Cookie categories we use</h2>

    <h3 class="block-title">Strictly necessary</h3>
    <p>These support basic site operation (such as remembering that you dismissed a notice). They cannot be switched off and are not used to track you across other sites.</p>

    <h3 class="block-title">Analytics</h3>
    <p>We use privacy-respecting analytics cookies to measure aggregated, non-identifying usage &mdash; which guides are read and in what region. This helps us improve the content. These cookies do not identify you personally.</p>

    <h3 class="block-title">Preferences</h3>
    <p>Where available, these remember choices you make (such as cookie consent) so you do not have to set them again on a later visit.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="topic-section">
    <h2>Managing your cookies</h2>
    <p>Most browsers let you view, block or delete cookies through their settings. Because the controls live in your browser rather than on this Site, the exact steps differ by browser; search your browser&rsquo;s help centre for &ldquo;cookies&rdquo; to find them. Blocking some cookies may affect how parts of the Site behave.</p>
    <p>For the broader privacy picture, see our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="topic-section">
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this Cookie Settings page as our use of cookies changes. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date at the top reflects the latest revision.</p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
